# Vocabulary (Chinese ↔ site)

| User says | Means |
|-----------|--------|
| **项目** | Project (`/projects`) |
| **见解** | Insight (`/insights`) |
| **第一个项目** | Full-width featured lead above the projects filter (`projectsFeaturedLead`) |
| **项目详情** | Project detail **copy** (文案), not the whole page chrome |

# 项目详情文案 — up to these four, in order

When the user supplies project detail copy (Word or chat), map it into the existing case detail UI (`ProjectCaseDemo` About panel / project-aware copy), **never invent a fifth chapter** and **never reorder**:

1. **Background**
2. **Challenge**
3. **What I did**
4. **Outcome**

## Missing chapters

- **Only render chapters the user actually provided.** If Outcome (or any other) is missing, **omit it entirely** — no placeholder text, no empty heading, no filler from `challenge` / `result` / `summary`.
- Source of truth: `getCaseCopySections` in `content/caseCopy.ts` filters empty bodies.

## Format rules

- Fit the **already shipped** detail template (dark page, Study The Project panel, title/body type styles) — do not revive the old always-on full-page chapter stack as a separate layout.
- Section labels match the four names above (casing as the user writes; default display follows site conventions / lowercase labels when filling from Word).
- Fill only what they provide; do not rewrite voice unless asked.

## Do not

- Swap section order
- Rename these four without an explicit user request
- Invent Outcome (or any chapter) when the user did not supply it
- Treat「项目详情」as layout/chrome work unless they also ask for UI changes

# Related projects

Match Insights: Related is **same type-tag only** (`project.tags` / involvement chip), not a random pool.

- Call `getRelatedProjects(exclude, limit, project.tags)`
- No same-tag peers → hide the Related strip (empty array)
- Do not fill with unrelated projects
